WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.863 --> 00:00:06.823
African continent.
More than a fifth of its one point three

00:00:06.893 --> 00:00:11.583
billion people don't have enough to eat.
With water shortages and extreme weather

00:00:11.583 --> 00:00:13.663
events being the main contributing
factors.

00:00:14.523 --> 00:00:18.633
Somalia, though, is at the epicenter of
this deepening climate and hunger crisis

00:00:18.633 --> 00:00:21.933
that is gripping most severely the East
Africa region.

00:00:22.683 --> 00:00:28.413
Bloomberg traveled to Gulf chaos in
central Somalia last month, where the

00:00:28.413 --> 00:00:30.513
impact of the worst drought to impact
the country in four decades was laid

00:00:30.513 --> 00:00:33.663
bare.
Vast tracts of countryside were

00:00:33.663 --> 00:00:38.613
transformed into barren wasteland.
Crops had been decimated and children

00:00:38.613 --> 00:00:42.093
were dying of starvation.
One woman named Hassan had lost five of

00:00:42.093 --> 00:00:45.753
her 10 children to starvation and
disease within the past year.

00:00:46.863 --> 00:00:50.853
After the drought wiped out most of her
family's goatherd, its main source of

00:00:50.853 --> 00:00:55.323
income.
Official data shows that 900 other

00:00:55.323 --> 00:00:57.453
children under the age of five have died
across Somalia since January.

00:00:57.603 --> 00:01:02.433
The true tally is unknown and unlikely,
exponentially higher because vast areas

00:01:02.433 --> 00:01:06.753
are under the control of al-Shabaab
insurgents and inaccessible to officials

00:01:06.773 --> 00:01:09.723
and aid workers in the area surrounding
Gul Kale.

00:01:13.413 --> 00:01:13.423
More than half of the children are
already considered malnourished

00:01:13.433 --> 00:01:19.353
Countrywide.
More than 350000 Somalian children have

00:01:19.353 --> 00:01:20.083
been treated for the condition this
year.

00:01:21.573 --> 00:01:26.973
Almost half of Somalia's 17 million
people are in urgent need of aid, and

00:01:26.973 --> 00:01:29.133
more than one million have abandoned
their homes in search of food and

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:31.983
grazing.
Rains have failed for five consecutive

00:01:31.983 --> 00:01:36.963
seasons, and water shortages are even
worse than in the early 1990s, when a

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:41.853
famine claimed about 260000 lives.
The UN expects a famine to be declared

00:01:41.853 --> 00:01:44.893
soon in three isolated regions of the
country.

